1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,650
A shared bill should end
with everyone

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,600
certain—and no one chasing screenshots.

3
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:09,150
FINALTab turns one receipt
into a deterministic ledger,

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,650
binds every debtor's USDC pull
to the entire payout plan,

5
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,650
then sends the exact call
through KeeperHub.

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,500
Scan a crowded receipt.

7
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:20,650
Correct any extraction.

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,600
Invite the table.

9
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:24,750
Describe who had what.

10
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,300
FINALTab reconciles every

11
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:28,950
line—tax, tip, and service
included—to the cent,

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,650
across the whole table.

13
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,500
The graph collapses many obligations
into a small, deterministic transfer set.

14
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:37,000
Freeze once, and the ledger hash,
settlement ID,

15
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:40,100
debits, payouts, chain, and contract

16
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:43,600
become one immutable plan.

17
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:46,750
Each debtor signs twice:

18
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,550
Circle's authorization
to pull their exact USDC,

19
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,300
and FINALTab consent
to the complete payout plan.

20
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:53,950
Then KeeperHub simulates.

21
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,550
A revert never broadcasts.

22
00:00:56,350 --> 00:00:58,250
Only after simulation

23
00:00:58,300 --> 00:00:59,650
and final human approval
does KeeperHub submit.

24
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,500
Green appears only when
its terminal receipt

25
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:05,700
matches an independent
Base Sepolia RPC check.

26
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:09,650
Agents get the same safety rail
through nine production MCP tools.

27
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:12,600
FINALTab never holds their wallet keys.

28
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:16,600
The agent allocates, prepares the V2 plan,
and returns typed data for every debtor.

29
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:20,450
It simulates, requests a short-lived
human-signed challenge, then submits.

30
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:24,100
The status call receives
three exact arguments:

31
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:27,150
execution ID, settlement ID,
and ledger hash.

32
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:30,550
Only the exact indexed event
resolves VERIFIED_SETTLED.

33
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:32,250
FINALTab.

34
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,150
One table.

35
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,000
One plan.

36
00:01:34,050 --> 00:01:34,800
KeeperHub executes.

37
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:35,500
Anyone can verify.
